<title>USA: U.S. farm-wheel tractor sales up 19 pct in October.</title>
<headline>U.S. farm-wheel tractor sales up 19 pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. sales of farm-wheel tractors rose 19.2 percent in October to 11,829 from 9,926 a year ago, said the Equipment Manufacturers Institute.</p>
<p>Year to date, the trade group said total sales rose eight percent to 98,946 from 91,655 in the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>In October, total two-wheel drive tractor sales increased 19 percent to 11,197 from 9,412 and four-wheel tractors rose 23 percent to 632 from 514.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
